00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.110
Jack: The Importance of
the different stages of the

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:06.149
software development lifecycle.

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:09.580
So, let’s review these stages and look
at their importance in more detail.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:15.120
The initial stages of requirement,
gather, and analysis are the key planning

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.170
stages where the requirements need
to be fully understood so as to know

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:20.540
what the client’s requirements are.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:24.950
These can be analysed in order to build
a strong foundation for the product.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.690
Leah: Careful analysis of the client’s
needs is necessary to make sure

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:31.419
that all requirements will be met.

00:00:32.019 --> 00:00:35.969
Misunderstandings at this stage could
result in wasted work and could be

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:40.919
costly so it is essential that the IT
team, often the Business Analyst and

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.290
the Project Manager, set up a meeting
with the client to gather all the

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:48.840
information like what they want to
build, who will be the end-user and

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.499
what is the purpose of the product.

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:54.970
For example, if the client needs
an application involving financial

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:59.110
transactions, they need to know what
these would involve, how they would be

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:01.350
done such as in what currencies etc.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:07.000
Jack: Once the requirements are clearly
understood, the SRS [Software Requirement

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.059
Specification] document is created, and
any analysis is carried out to check the

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.230
development achievability of the product.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:19.230
The analysis breaks the project
down into clearly defined tasks and

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:23.430
outlines the responsibilities of
each department at each stage through

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.000
to the delivery of the product.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.929
It will also focus on time frames
and costing associated with

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:30.220
the development of the product.

00:01:31.119 --> 00:01:34.190
Leah: The next design stage
involves designing the system

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:38.259
architecture that will be used for
implementing the system development.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:42.590
This phase will detail, the
necessary specifications, features

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.389
and operations that will satisfy
the functional requirements of

00:01:46.389 --> 00:01:47.769
the proposed software product.

00:01:48.639 --> 00:01:52.789
End users and software engineering
professionals will consider the essential

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:57.880
components [hardware and/or software]
structure [networking capabilities],

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:02.200
processing and procedures for the
system to accomplish its objectives.

00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:07.060
At this stage the external design may
also be considered, and any mock-ups made.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.290
Jack: Once all the planning and design
stages are completed the development

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.290
or implementation stage begins.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.830
Developers will start coding carefully
following any software requirements and

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:22.669
specifications in the SRS document as
well as internal design instructions.

00:02:23.299 --> 00:02:27.520
All the components of the software
are implemented in this stage and if

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:31.140
the guidelines have all been followed
this should proceed without problems.

00:02:32.059 --> 00:02:35.530
Most of the time actions may
involve writing totally new code

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.539
and developing a totally new system.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:42.510
But sometimes actions may involve moving
data and components from an old system

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:44.230
and placing them in the new system.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:49.709
Any developments done to an existing
system will need to be done out of peak

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.040
business hours to minimise disruptions.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:57.309
Leah: The ‘testing’ phase always starts
when the coding is completed, and the

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.690
product modules are released for testing.

00:03:00.109 --> 00:03:03.680
In this phase, the developed software
is tested thoroughly, and any

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.750
defects or bugs found are assigned
to developers to get them fixed.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:13.150
Test engineers will perform various types
of functional and non-functional testing

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:19.250
related to core applications, text input,
security and scalability issues if needed.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:23.190
Retesting is also done until
the point at which the software

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:25.090
meets the client’s expectations.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:30.220
Testers will refer to the SRS document
to make sure that the software

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.239
is as per the client’s standard.

00:03:33.349 --> 00:03:36.339
Jack: Once the testing is over
and the software demonstrated to

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:39.520
be ‘working’ it can be deployed
in the business environment.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:45.760
However, User Acceptance Testing
[UAT] may need to be carried out

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:49.620
first before final deployment in a
replica of the intended environment.

00:03:50.849 --> 00:03:54.469
The client along with the developers
can test the system before it

00:03:54.469 --> 00:03:56.500
is signed off and goes ‘live’

00:03:57.490 --> 00:04:02.640
Leah: Even after deployment as the
client uses the software issues may arise

00:04:02.679 --> 00:04:04.589
or enhancements may need to be made.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:08.609
The software developers will be
responsible for maintaining the system.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:12.549
They will also be called upon to
produce updates and monitor any

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.210
issues that may arise in the future.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:19.380
Jack: The software development life cycle
approach to creating software can be a

00:04:19.399 --> 00:04:24.380
time-consuming process, but if it is done
correctly, it should run quite smoothly.

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:28.789
Some steps are more difficult than others
but should not be rushed or overlooked,

00:04:29.109 --> 00:04:32.380
as an oversight can prevent an entire
system from functioning properly.

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:37.159
Understanding the different stages of
the process is important and essential

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:41.650
to successful planning, design, and
implementation of all software systems.

